cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use procgrep in research, please cite both the software and
  the paper it was extracted from.
title: "procgrep: Procedural fingerprinting of LLM coding-agent rollouts"
abstract: >-
  procgrep canonicalizes heterogeneous LLM agent traces into a shared
  atom alphabet, learns a BPE procedure vocabulary, encodes trajectories
  as procedure-frequency distributions, and supports cross-group
  comparison via Jensen-Shannon divergence, leave-one-group-out
  predictive probes, UMAP projection, and pattern matching. Post-hoc
  analysis only; no model calls.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Oderinwale
    given-names: Hamidah
repository-code: "https://github.com/hamidahoderinwale/procgrep"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.3"
keywords:
  - llm
  - coding-agents
  - procedural-fingerprinting
  - bpe
  - jensen-shannon-divergence
  - trace-analysis
  - controlled-evaluation
preferred-citation:
